  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Agribusiness innovation and sustainable entrepreneurship in South Africa (InnoGiyani)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The private sector, specifically SPAR, the Manombe Cooperative Trust, and farmers are prepared to invest in production and marketing once innovative niche products are identified and entrepreneurship capacity is built among smallholder farms to become business partners. South Africa has a free-market system, but small farmers located far from urban centres face significant challenges due to the scale of their operations. The Giyani region, having the best soils and a tropical climate, is known for its difficult socio-economic and agro-hydrological conditions. To foster development in this region, innovative agri-business strategies are necessary, such as identifying niche products that can be grown profitably in these conditions. Building up the related capacity in innovating agri-business implies that the project cannot be commercial from scratch. Investing in a Public Private Partnership to establish an innovation facility will result in several benefits to facilitate sustainable entrepreneurship in the future. The project builds on a European Union Seventh Framework (EU FP7) research programme to isolate primary innovations through a trans-disciplinary participatory process.</narrative>
  </description>
